  "data": {
    "body": "A system consists of a two concentric disks -  a smaller uniform disk of mass, \\textbf{m} = 1.60 \\textbf{kg} and radius, \\textbf{r} = 0.12 \\textbf{m} and a larger uniform disk of mass, \\textbf{M} = 4 \\textbf{kg} and radius \\textbf{R} = 0.30 \\textbf{m}. Force $\\mathbf{F}_2$ = 60 \\textbf{N} acts tangentially (i.e. perpendicular to the radius) on the outer disk, and Force $\\mathbf{F}_1$ = 36.00 \\textbf{N} acts tangentially on the inner disk as shown.\n\nWhat is the \\textbf{angular acceleration} of the system about the axis? Note: The moment of inertia of a disk is $I$ = $\\frac{1} {2} MR^2$",
